# Nissan Micra K10 three-door hatchback, 1983-1992.
#
# The first Micra: the upright hatch, the flat waistline pressing along the
# flank, the near-vertical tail and the black rubbing strip at door-handle
# height. Sold in Britain from 1983. The five-door body is not represented,
# because no usable five-door side, front or rear photograph was found.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Micra
#
# Dimensions 3.785 x 1.560 x 1.395 m, wheelbase 2.300 m (Wikipedia infobox,
# not checked against a Nissan document).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-level side photograph of a UK car. Its
# suspension is lowered and its wheels are non-standard, but the body shell,
# glass and door apertures are standard and are what is modelled.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK colour list was found. White, Red, Blue and Silver
# are plain names, not factory paint names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 145 km/h. Comfort 50/405, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 50. Classes 0,1.
# Dates: intro 1983, the month being unconfirmed and set to January; retire
# staggered 1999-2003 as a road tail, the K10 being long-lived as a used car.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k10.dae. References:
# citycars/references/nissan-micra-k10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the early front and the mid-1980s rear represent the
# generation between them. The bumper corners and the lamp joins are
# simplified and visibly faceted in close views.


obj=citycar
